      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Bar plots\n",
        "\n",
        "We can create bar plots of our data by setting `kind='bar'` in the `plot()` method.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, let's say we want to get data about the 10 penguins with the lowest body mass. We can first select this data using the `nsmallest()` method for series:"
      ],
      "id": "a9cd9dc0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "smallest = penguins['body_mass_g'].nsmallest(10)\n",
        "smallest"
      ],
      "id": "e9c7ac2a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "We can then plot this data as a bar plot:"
      ],
      "id": "9ded334c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "smallest.plot(kind='bar')"
      ],
      "id": "6c6633bd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "If we wanted to look at other data for these smallest penguins we can use a different call to the `nsmallest` method:"
      ],
      "id": "9514faf8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "penguins.nsmallest(10, 'body_mass_g')"
      ],
      "id": "34bf10c5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
